  "title": "Provider-neutral tracker seam and the GitHub adapter",
  "summary": "Adds a provider-neutral `Tracker` seam to the osf crate — a trait, its data types, the ready rule, the run-finishing writes, and an in-memory test double — plus the first adapter, `GitHubTracker`, which drives GitHub Issues and Projects v2 through the installed `gh` CLI. Every request is one `gh` invocation whose argv and JSON payload are built by pure functions and whose response is read by a pure parser, so the adapter is a thin loop over a `GhRunner`. A neutrality test asserts the seam's own source names no provider.",
